

Ticket reference number
INC001

Incident title
Outlook unable to send or receive emails

User and department
User: Sipho Nkosi
Department: Finance
Affected Service: Microsoft 365 Exchange Online / Outlook Desktop

Reported symptoms
- Outlook shows "Disconnected" / "Work Offline"
- Unable to send or receive emails in Outlook desktop
- Outlook Web (OWA) works fine at outlook.office.com
- Issue after password prompt
- Colleague on same network works normally

Business impact and priority
- Priority: P2 - High
- Impact: Finance month-end reporting delayed
- Scope: Single user, not service-wide
- Service Health: Exchange Online healthy

Initial troubleshooting
1. Scope check: Only one user affected, colleague in Finance works
2. Service Health: admin.microsoft.com > Health > Service health > Exchange Online - No issues
3. Network check: Internet working, Teams and OneDrive working
4. Outlook status: Bottom bar shows Work Offline enabled, Account shows Need Password

Investigation findings
- Entra ID Sign-in logs KQL: SigninLogs | where UserPrincipalName == "sipho@domain.com" | where Result != 0
- Finding: Failure 50053 - User authentication failure, token expired
- Credential Manager: Control Panel > Credential Manager > Found old MicrosoftOffice16 credential
- dsregcmd /status: AzureAdJoined YES, SSO State AzureAdPr
- OWA test: Login successful, can send/receive - Confirms mailbox healthy, issue is client only

Root cause
Stale MFA token plus cached old credentials in Windows Credential Manager after password refresh plus Outlook Work Offline mode enabled.

Resolution steps
GUI:
- Outlook > Send/Receive > Uncheck Work Offline
- Control Panel > Credential Manager > Remove MicrosoftOffice credentials
- Outlook > File > Office Account > Sign out > Close Outlook
- Re-open Outlook > Sign-in with M365 account > Complete MFA > Connected

PowerShell Verification:
```powershell
Connect-ExchangeOnline
Get-Mailbox -Identity sipho@domain.com | Select DisplayName, PrimarySmtpAddress
Test-MailboxConnectivity -Identity sipho@domain.com
Connect-MgGraph -Scopes User.Read.All
Get-MgUser -UserId sipho@domain.com | fl DisplayName, AccountEnabled
Verification and testing
- Sent test email to self - Delivered
- Received email from colleague - Appeared in Inbox
- Sent email with attachment - Success
- Monitored 30 minutes - No re-prompt

User communication
